	Configure a signal path to add in another signal
apifn	sm_path_mix
params	sm_path_mix_parms mixp
	The signal path to be configured
field	tSMPathId path in
	Enables (non-zero) or disables (zero) adding another signal
	to the input signal.
field   tSM_INT enable in
	The datafeed which is the signal to be added. Only used if
ref	enable
	is non-zero.
field   tSMDatafeedId mixin in
	Volume adjustment (dB).
field	tSM_INT volume in
unstruct
	Configures signal mixing on a signal path.
	The specified signal is added into the signal being processed
	by this path, and the result is adjusted according to the
ref	volume
	parameter, which has a range of at least -24 to +8 dB.
	Typically, the signal is adjusted by -6 dB to prevent the sum
	of the two signals being louder than each original signal.
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  gainbg.
explain
	0
retval

	Configure a signal path to convert signal to a different sampling rate
apifn	sm_path_resample
params	sm_path_resample_parms resamplep
	The signal path to be configured
field	tSMPathId path in
	Sets the up-sampling ratio. This value must be in the range 1..6.
field   tSM_INT uprate in
	Sets the down-sampling ratio. This value must be in the range 1..6.
field   tSM_INT downrate in
unstruct
	Configures sample rate conversion on a signal path. If
ref	uprate
	and
ref	downrate
	are equal, sample rate conversion is disabled. Otherwise the
	signal is converted to a sampling rate of
ref	uprate
	/
ref	downrate
	times the original sampling rate. For example, if
ref	uprate
	is two, and
ref	downrate
	is one, the sampling rate is doubled. To produce the best audio quality,
	and to use the least processor time,
ref	uprate
	should always be kept as small as possible. For example,
ref	uprate
	= 2, with
ref	downrate
	= 3, would decrease the sampling rate to two-thirds of the original
	value, but so would
ref	uprate
	= 4, with
ref	downrate
	= 6. Both the audio quality and the CPU loading will be noticeably better
	with
ref	uprate
	= 2, than with
ref	uprate
	= 4.
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  resample.
explain
	0
retval

	Obtain a datafeed from a signal path
apifn	sm_path_get_datafeed
params	sm_path_datafeed_parms datafeedp
	The signal path from which to obtain a datafeed
field	tSMPathId path in
	The datafeed object representing the processed signal from
	the signal path
field	tSMDatafeedId datafeed out
unstruct
	Request a datafeed identifier from a signal path. This identifer
	can subsequently be used in a call to 
fnref	sm_channel_datafeed_connect,
fnref	sm_tdmtx_datafeed_connect
	or
fnref	sm_vmptx_datafeed_connect
	to connect the result of the signal path procesing to a speech
	channel (tSMChannelId), TDM[tx], or a VMP[tx]
	respectively. It is valid until the path is destroyed.
	Datafeed connections can only be made between objects allocated
	on the same <code>tSMModuleId</code>.
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref	datafeed
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

