	Determine path status
apifn	sm_path_status
params	sm_path_status_parms statusp
	The path to interrogate
field	tSMPathId path in
enumstart kSMPathStatus
	Indicates that there is nothing significant to report.
enum	kSMPathStatusRunning
	Tone detector reports ongoing tone or silence.
enum	kSMPathStatusOngoingTone
	Tone detector reports previously ongoing tone or silence has completed.
enum	kSMPathStatusEndTone
	Indicates that the path has stopped and can be destroyed.
enum	kSMPathStatusStopped
enumend status out
	Additional information relating to the current status of the path 
union
	This field is only valid if the status is either
ref	kSMPathStatusOngoingTone
	or
ref kSMPathStatusEndTone.
struct
	The id for the recognised tone (or zero if silence).
field	tSM_INT id out
	The ongoing or final duration of the tone or silence.
field	unsigned duration out
unstruct	tone
unstruct	u
unstruct
	Returns the current status of the path or an error to indicate that
	a problem occurred.
	<p>
	When the event, obtained from
fnref	sm_path_get_event,
	is signalled the user must call this function to determine the nature
	of the status change. The change in status may indicate that an error 
	occurred whilst processing a user request or it may be notifiying the 
	user of a change to the previous state of the path.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error	ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - if insufficient resources existed to create the path

	Obtain an event for a path
apifn	sm_path_get_event
params	sm_path_event_parms eventp
	The path 
field	tSMPathId path in
	The event identifier
field	tSMEventId event out
unstruct
	If the call completes successfully 
ref	event
	will hold the tSMEventId belonging to 
ref	path.
	The tSMEventId is valid until the path is destroyed using 
fnref	sm_path_destroy.
	This event will be signalled when a status change occurs on the 
	path. When the event is signalled the user must call 
fnref	sm_path_status
	to discover the nature of the status change.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Connect a datafeed to a signal path
apifn	sm_path_datafeed_connect
params	sm_path_datafeed_connect_parms datafeedp
	The signal path that will receive and process the data
field	tSMPathId path in
	The datafeed acting as a source of data for the signal path
field	tSMDatafeedId data_source in
unstruct
	Connects a datafeed to a signal path. The
ref	data_source
	must be a datafeed obtained from 
fnref	sm_channel_get_datafeed,
fnref	sm_tdmrx_get_datafeed
fnref	sm_vmprx_get_datafeed
	or 
fnref	sm_path_get_datafeed.
	Datafeed connections can only be made between objects allocated
	on the same <code>tSMModuleId</code>.
	The signal path
ref	path
	will receive any data that is generated by the output task from which 
ref	data_source
	was derived.
	<p>
	To disconnect a signal path from a datafeed, specify 
	<code>kSMNullDatafeedId</code> as the tSMDatafeedId in
ref	data_source
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref	datafeed
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval

