	Configure a signal path to apply a filter to emphasise or deemphasise high frequencies
apifn	sm_path_emphasis
params	sm_path_emphasis_parms emphparms
	The signal path to be configured
field	tSMPathId path in
	Enables (non-zero) or disables (zero) filter.
field	tSM_INT enable in
	Indicates what mode the filter operates in.
enumstart kSMPathEmphMode
	Puts the filter into HF emphasis mode.
enum	kSMPathEmphModeHFEmphasis
	Puts the filter into HF de-emphasis mode.
enum	kSMPathEmphModeHFDeemphasis
enumend mode in
	Extra gain to apply to the signal as part of the filter, in dB.
field	tSM_INT gain in
unstruct
	Configures a high-frequency emphasis/de-emphasis filter.
	In emphasis mode, response curve is approximately -3dB at 0Hz rising
	to 0dB at 300Hz and 20dB at 3330Hz.
	In de-emphasis mode, the inverse filter is applied: 3dB at 0Hz falling
	to 0dB at 300Hz and -20dB at 3330Hz.
	Disabling the filter also disables the gain.
	Note that the frequencies quoted are proportional to the input signal sample rate 
	and those given are for an input signal sample rate of 8000 samples per second. 
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  emph
	to be loaded.
explain
	0
retval

	Configure a signal path to detect and optionally eliminate tones
apifn	sm_path_tonedetect
params	sm_path_tonedetect_parms tdparms
	The signal path to be configured
field	tSMPathId path in
	Enables (non-zero) or disables (zero) elimination of detected tones from signal.
field	tSM_INT elim in
	Tone detection mode - see 
fnref	sm_listen_for
	for more details.
enumstart kSMPathToneDetectMode
	Tone detection disabled.
enum	kSMPathToneDetectModeNone
	Simple tone detection enabled, no minimum period.
enum	kSMPathToneDetectModeMinDurationNoMinimum
	Robust detection of tones with duration as short as 40mS.
enum	kSMPathToneDetectModeMinDuration40
	Simple tone detection enabled, tone must be valid for 64ms to be detected.
enum	kSMPathToneDetectModeMinDuration64
enumend min_duration in
	Selects tone set used for tone detection - use same as for active_tone_set_id field in
fnref	sm_listen_for.
field	tSM_INT tone_set_id in
unstruct
	Configures a tone detector on signal path.
	Detected tones are reported through 
fnref	sm_path_status.
	Tones that are detected may optionally be eliminated.
	When eliminating tones, the signal is delayed by small amount so entire 
	tone can be eliminated.
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  td
	to be loaded.
explain
	0
retval

	Instructs a path to stop all processing
apifn	sm_path_stop
params	sm_path_stop_parms stopp
	A tSMPathId that has been previously created by a call to
fnref	sm_path_create.
field	tSMPathId path in
unstruct
	Requests that a path stops executing. The user will be notified that
	a path has terminated by a final status, kSMPAthStatusStopped, from
fnref	sm_path_status.
	Once the stopped status notification has been received the path can 
	be destroyed using
fnref	sm_path_destroy.
	<p>
	Once the path has stopped the event should no longer be used to wait
	for status notifications as it will be signalled permanently. The event
	is invalidated when
fnref	sm_path_destroy
	is called.
explain
	0
retval
